{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Accident-Prone in Egypt"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Accident "}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 11}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling ."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling ."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling ."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling ."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling ."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling ."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes a brief text about the advantages and disadvantages of specific forms of communication through the appropriate use of grammar, vocabulary, syntaxes and spelling ."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le11ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Past tense and Past Continuous tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished.<br>You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular.<br> Regular verbs end in -ed or -ied.<br> Irregular verbs change in different ways.<br> For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary did followed by the verb in the base form, like Did you ask \u2026 ?<br> Did is the past form of to do.<br>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For Past Continuous, we add was/were + verb\u201cing\u201d to verbs.  Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add \u201cing\u201d."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Present \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" talk\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" talked  \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were talking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" walk   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"walked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were walking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" focus \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"focused \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were focusing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" lead\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" led \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were leading\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" return \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"returned \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were returning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" have \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"had \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were having\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" swerve \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"swerved \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were swerving\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The driver was swerving through the busy, congested streets when we came across a frightening accident."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We were driving between the hotel and the museum when we saw a lot of men arguing on the street."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hectic "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very busy and filled with activity "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The hectic streets were filled with people, cars and wagons."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you can use to describe an accident."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "congested "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " too full or crowded with something  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The streets were so congested that the cars could not move."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conscious "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "awake and able to understand what is happening around you "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The young boy was conscious."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gash "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a long, deep cut "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was a gash on his lower leg."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bundled"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to send someone to a place quickly or suddenly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We bundled up the boy and placed him the car."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to swerve "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to change direction suddenly "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The car was swerving on the road."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "calf "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the back part of the leg below the knee  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There was a large cut on the back of his calf."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to wrap"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to cover something by folding a piece of material around it "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One of the tourists wrapped up his gash with a tee-shirt."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le11ob08aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write a 80-100 word e-mail about an accident."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use adjectives to describe the event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 1 sentence that uses the Past Continuous tense and the Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Include paragraph structure."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the paragraph aloud to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph about an accident."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use adjectives to describe an event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use the Past Continuous tense and the Past tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I read my paragraph to a partner."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le11ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le11ob08re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn5le11ob08re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "Dear Vanessa,<br><br>I have to tell you about our experience on the hectic streets of Cairo!", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn5le11ob08re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "The driver was swerving through the busy, congested streets when we came across a frightening accident.", "id": 2, "time": "6000", "image": "engenn5le11ob08re2img01.jpg"}, {"text": "A young boy was lying on the road.  He was conscious but not moving. His mother was sitting beside him, crying and holding his head as we arrived.  People were gathered around.  The driver of the car who hit the boy was having an argument with a group of men. My driver stopped to help.  The child looked up at us and pointed 